;; bnei.dev — BIND zone file for Cloudflare's "Import DNS records"
;;
;; Generated 2026-08-11 from the live googledomains-hosted zone (ADR-0032).
;; See docs/runbooks/dns-cloudflare-migration.md for the cutover procedure.
;;
;; SOA and apex NS are deliberately omitted — Cloudflare manages both, and
;; including them makes the importer complain.
;;
;; The 4 A records below replace 19 flat per-host records. DNS wildcards match
;; exactly one label (RFC 4592), which is why `*.ente` and `*.e2e` are separate
;; entries rather than being covered by `*`.
;;
;; TTL 300 is the cutover value — raise it once the migration is confirmed.
;;
;; !! After importing, set all four A records to DNS-only (grey cloud). !!
;; A proxied record terminates TLS at Cloudflare's edge, which breaks Traefik's
;; TLS-ALPN-01 renewal for that host — silently, up to 90 days later.

$TTL 300

bnei.dev.                  300  IN  A    82.65.231.50
*.bnei.dev.                300  IN  A    82.65.231.50
*.ente.bnei.dev.           300  IN  A    82.65.231.50
*.e2e.bnei.dev.            300  IN  A    82.65.231.50

bnei.dev.                  300  IN  MX   10 mxa.mailgun.org.
bnei.dev.                  300  IN  MX   10 mxb.mailgun.org.

bnei.dev.                  300  IN  TXT  "v=spf1 include:mailgun.org ~all"

;; DKIM. The literal space in the middle of the key is NOT a TXT chunk
;; boundary — the payload is a single 226-byte character-string, under the
;; 255-byte limit. RFC 6376 has verifiers ignore whitespace inside `p=`, so it
;; is harmless, but reproduce it byte-for-byte rather than "cleaning it up".
smtp._domainkey.bnei.dev.  300  IN  TXT  "k=rsa; p=MIGfMA0GCSqGSIb3DQEBAQUAA4GNADCBiQKBgQDnmObaHwGAPisYQLI5IWp4OcjFxQBQ7n2wfS0BRFXhJzhd8uV3J1TPq8v/xU20VC8sVeAC70oL8JB2gV2X4fBg1PXxPH+9FmVZmTYRvEXCrHRujic7I/YMj8dTMGBA0ZTokCLxFR4lZBWvpQdvBosHBKg3 l5orSRvm+peemf1GAQIDAQAB"
